WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:22.000
hope Alpha is able to scan Sandville for other alien life-forms," Ally thought, racing into the house.

2
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.844
"I need to find out if Melanie is from Earth—or another galaxy!"

3
00:00:26.864 --> 00:00:31.488
"Ally!" Mateo hurried toward her, smiling from ear to ear.

4
00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.152
"I've got big news!"

5
00:00:33.172 --> 00:00:36.633
"Did you find me a less expensive plane ticket?"

6
00:00:37.093 --> 00:00:38.174
Ally asked hopefully.

7
00:00:38.194 --> 00:00:41.615
"Sorry, not yet," Mateo said.

8
00:00:41.635 --> 00:00:47.476
"But I did find out that UserPFM5 lives in Sandville.

9
00:00:48.036 --> 00:00:50.157
I'm trying to figure out the person's real name.

10
00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:56.018
When I do, I'm going to ask UserPFM5 to sell the Cosmic Quest comic to me."

11
00:00:56.038 --> 00:01:02.557
"Someone else's real identity has to be figured out," Ally mumbled.

12
00:01:03.477 --> 00:01:04.818
Mateo looked confused.

13
00:01:04.838 --> 00:01:06.579
"What do you mean?"

14
00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:09.601
"Nothing." Ally shook her head.

15
00:01:09.621 --> 00:01:14.885
"I don't want to bother Mateo with my suspicions about Melanie yet," she thought.

16
00:01:14.905 --> 00:01:17.187
"He has enough on his mind."

17
00:01:17.207 --> 00:01:20.729
"That sounds like a good plan," she said.

18
00:01:20.749 --> 00:01:23.351
"I have to go check on Alpha right now."

19
00:01:23.371 --> 00:01:29.415
"Oh! Maybe later she can help me figure out who UserPFM5 is," Mateo said.

20
00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:30.916
Ally nodded.

21
00:01:31.828 --> 00:01:33.349
"Sure. We can try it."

22
00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:37.512
When Ally entered her room, Alpha's screen was lit.

23
00:01:37.532 --> 00:01:39.353
"Greetings, Allyzooba.

24
00:01:39.874 --> 00:01:41.115
Alpha reporting for duty.

25
00:01:41.655 --> 00:01:42.616
All systems go."

26
00:01:42.636 --> 00:01:46.358
"Yes!" Ally cheered.

27
00:01:46.378 --> 00:01:49.160
"You're working—at last!

28
00:01:50.101 --> 00:01:51.742
And I have another job for you.

29
00:01:52.443 --> 00:01:56.225
I need you to scan Sandville for other alien life-forms."

30
00:01:56.245 --> 00:01:59.808
"Affirmative." Alpha's screen blinked once.

31
00:02:00.488 --> 00:02:02.770
"Alien life-form located in the park."

32
00:02:03.771 --> 00:02:04.792
Ally's heart pounded.

33
00:02:04.812 --> 00:02:07.315
"Show me on the screen, please."

34
00:02:08.836 --> 00:02:10.358
A live feed of the park appeared.

35
00:02:10.838 --> 00:02:13.741
There were people walking, Rollerblading, and picnicking.

36
00:02:14.702 --> 00:02:19.727
Ally spotted Phil and Tina chatting on a bench, but there was no sign of Melanie's purple hair.

37
00:02:20.448 --> 00:02:24.592
Suddenly Alpha zoomed in on a rock near the bench where Phil and Tina were sitting.

38
00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:30.604
"Detected: remnants of a comet that broke up approximately five hundred Earth years ago."

39
00:02:30.624 --> 00:02:32.445
"A rock?"

40
00:02:33.126 --> 00:02:34.487
Ally's eyes went wide.

41
00:02:34.507 --> 00:02:38.590
"Are you sure that's the alien life-form?"

42
00:02:39.431 --> 00:02:40.071
Alpha frowned.

43
00:02:40.091 --> 00:02:46.596
"Certainty is only at 85 percent because of the primitive Earth technology that I am housed in."

44
00:02:46.616 --> 00:02:49.598
"I'll take 85 percent!"

45
00:02:50.118 --> 00:02:51.059
Ally wiped her brow.

46
00:02:51.079 --> 00:02:55.931
"Phew! I guess Melanie is as human as everyone else in town.

47
00:02:56.912 --> 00:02:59.073
Okay, back to my other problem.

48
00:02:59.974 --> 00:03:04.458
You were going to figure out how to get me to Patagonia for a lot less than two

49
00:03:04.538 --> 00:03:05.639
thousand dollars."

50
00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:08.261
"Understood." Alpha blinked.

51
00:03:08.281 --> 00:03:13.866
"Lainie Polk is currently involved in a study of penguins in—" "I don't want to hear about her!"

52
00:03:14.286 --> 00:03:15.347
Ally covered her ears.

53
00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:20.531
"I need to figure out a way to get to Patagonia, otherwise I won't—" "Allyzooba!"

54
00:03:20.891 --> 00:03:21.552
Alpha snapped.

55
00:03:22.124 --> 00:03:24.305
"You are acting as impatient as an Earthling.

56
00:03:24.765 --> 00:03:26.806
Polk's research is in Patagonia."

57
00:03:27.786 --> 00:03:28.247
"It is?"

58
00:03:28.927 --> 00:03:29.787
Ally bit her lip.

59
00:03:29.807 --> 00:03:31.828
"That's a funny coincidence."

60
00:03:32.869 --> 00:03:34.529
"There is nothing humorous about it.

61
00:03:34.949 --> 00:03:36.710
Polk owns five private jets."

62
00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:41.152
"That's nice for her, if a bit much," Ally said.

63
00:03:41.172 --> 00:03:43.213
"You are not computing.

64
00:03:43.773 --> 00:03:44.874
She owes you a favor.

65
00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.415
Ask her to fly you to Patagonia."

66
00:03:47.435 --> 00:03:50.356
"Alpha, you're a genius!"

67
00:03:51.184 --> 00:03:53.766
Ally threw her arms around Alpha.

68
00:03:53.846 --> 00:03:54.346
Beep! Beep!

69
00:03:54.847 --> 00:03:56.748
"Allyzooba!" Alpha snapped.

70
00:03:56.768 --> 00:03:58.869
"That is not appropriate behavior!

71
00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:00.050
Unhand me!"

72
00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.312
"Fine." Ally backed away.

73
00:04:03.332 --> 00:04:05.854
"I'll just say thank you then."

74
00:04:05.874 --> 00:04:08.215
"That is acceptable."

75
00:04:09.696 --> 00:04:11.398
Ally dialed Lainie Polk's office.

76
00:04:13.059 --> 00:04:14.580
"Hi, this is Ally.

77
00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.941
Can you connect me to Lainie, please?"

78
00:04:17.422 --> 00:04:18.042
Ally asked.

79
00:04:18.062 --> 00:04:19.443
"Hi, Ally.

80
00:04:19.543 --> 00:04:22.233
She's difficult to reach," the assistant said.

81
00:04:22.253 --> 00:04:26.196
"In fact, you're the one who's responsible for her latest project.

82
00:04:26.736 --> 00:04:31.419
After she went to Sandville, she got very involved in saving different bird species.

83
00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.363
Currently she's in Patagonia working to save the habitat of the penguins."

84
00:04:36.383 --> 00:04:40.345
"Yes, I heard about that," Ally said.

85
00:04:40.365 --> 00:04:41.786
"That's why I'm calling.

86
00:04:42.227 --> 00:04:44.528
I would love to know more about her research."

87
00:04:45.269 --> 00:04:49.372
"I'm sure she'll be happy to tell you about it when she's back," the assistant said.

88
00:04:49.916 --> 00:04:51.437
"She's due back next fall."

89
00:04:51.637 --> 00:04:54.939
"What?" Ally almost shrieked into the phone.

90
00:04:55.659 --> 00:04:58.381
"Oh, well, uh, I can't wait that long!

91
00:04:59.001 --> 00:05:01.783
I'd really like to see it for myself—and soon!"

92
00:05:01.803 --> 00:05:04.584
"You want to go to Patagonia?"

93
00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:06.085
"I sure do!"

94
00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:07.026
Ally said.

95
00:05:07.046 --> 00:05:12.489
"Well, I'll get a message to her and see what she thinks," the assistant said.

96
00:05:12.509 --> 00:05:14.210
"When would you want to go?"

97
00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:17.151
"In a couple of days," Ally said.

98
00:05:17.171 --> 00:05:20.281
"Oh!" The assistant sounded surprised.

99
00:05:21.021 --> 00:05:22.582
"That's very soon.

100
00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.664
Then again, she does owe you an adventure.

101
00:05:26.284 --> 00:05:28.125
Let me try to get in touch with her.

102
00:05:28.665 --> 00:05:30.686
I'll call you back when I have an answer."

103
00:05:30.706 --> 00:05:31.987
"Thank you."

104
00:05:33.107 --> 00:05:35.969
Ally hung up and crossed her fingers on both hands.

105
00:05:35.989 --> 00:05:38.970
"Oh please, Lainie," she whispered.

106
00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.512
"You're my only hope!"
